& [SJS]
  + Situation: P0 prevents low-capacity startup but clean workspace builds can consume more than its threshold and it cannot observe the reserve after Cargo begins
  + Justification: a verifier that can itself exhaust the machine weakens the evidence boundary and makes its offline diagnostic unusable during the fault state
  + Solution: separate plan status startup admission and runtime reserve then reduce unnecessary artifacts and guard the running child with a fail-closed host-volume monitor

& [CompletedWorkSupportReview]
  + P0 already closes actions distribution target syntax repository identity serialization remote and destructive boundaries
  + P0 already uses one stable WSL target one build job and one test thread
  + P0 proof remains historical evidence for profile 0.1 and is not rewritten
  + P1 may evolve the same script path only under a new 0.2 profile and explicit source-linked phase lock
  + P1 does not reopen Cantor product runtime package trust semantic query or provider behavior

& [Delineation]
  + plan-only reports observed capacity but starts no child and returns success
  + Execute converts insufficient startup capacity into a pre-child fault
  + startup minimum is admission headroom while runtime reserve is the floor that must remain
  + lean Cargo profile changes artifact debug and incremental storage only and does not omit tests features targets or warnings
  + live guard observes the Windows volume that owns the repository from its exact WSL mount
  + guard failure interruption and child status are operational outcomes not product-test assertions
  + cache cleanup VHD compaction sparse mode and configuration mutation remain outside

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [input] action distribution target startup minimum reserve monitor interval Execute and repository volume free bytes
  + [derived] capacity_sufficient Windows drive WSL volume mount reserve bytes exact Bash command and declared environment
  + [output] one JSON plan plus optional guarded child outcome
  + [freshness] capacity is sampled once for the plan and repeatedly by the admitted child guard
  + [failure] invalid parameters unreadable sample startup insufficiency runtime reserve breach missing distribution or child failure refuse
  + [side_effect] only explicit Execute may create or update stable Cargo target temp and Python shim build artifacts

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + Master view: verification must preserve enough machine capacity to remain an observer rather than become the fault it is trying to inspect
  + Emissary view: forty-GiB startup minimum eight-GiB reserve two-second monitor one target and zero-debug nonincremental Cargo settings make that boundary testable
  + correction: a startup estimate alone is not a bound because clean dependency graphs and virtual-disk allocation vary
  + reconciliation: retain conservative admission and add a runtime guard that reacts to actual free bytes

& [SecurityAndHonesty]
  + plan capacity status never implies Execute authority
  + low capacity is visible in JSON and cannot be hidden by plan success
  + runtime sample parse failure interrupts rather than silently disabling the guard
  + reserve breach has a distinct status from Cargo test or linker failure
  + inputs interpolated into Bash remain closed conservative values or derived drive identity
  + no automatic cleanup follows any failure

& [Premortem]
  + failure: plan mode becomes environment-dependent; mitigation never throw capacity in plan-only mode
  + failure: guard watches WSL root rather than Windows backing volume; mitigation derive and expose /mnt/<drive> from repository volume
  + failure: df output is localized or malformed; mitigation LC_ALL=C numeric admission and fail-closed parse handling
  + failure: child finishes between kill check and sample; mitigation tolerate absent PID and preserve final wait status
  + failure: Cargo descendants survive interrupt; mitigation signal Cargo parent and retain no claim of process-group hard kill in P1
  + failure: lean settings change selected tests; mitigation keep exact Cargo selection unchanged and assert only artifact-profile variables differ
  + failure: threshold values reverse; mitigation require startup minimum strictly exceeds runtime reserve

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 preserves the two capacity incidents and P0 identities
  + fold_2 separates plan observation execution admission runtime reserve and product results
  + fold_3 models closed parameters derived capacity state guard states and distinct faults
  + fold_4 traces Windows drive to WSL mount and caller thresholds to exact bytes
  + fold_5 prunes cleanup compaction reconfiguration remote product runtime and semantic authority
  + fold_6 adds low-capacity plan impossible execute invalid relation guard text and parse tests
  + fold_7 converges on one evolved wrapper one offline suite documentation solution proof and rollback
  + [exhaustion_state] ready_for_P1_canonical_formation_and_phase_lock

& [Decision]
  + authorize only plan capacity status startup-versus-reserve validation lean artifact variables and one WSL runtime reserve guard
  + default MinimumFreeGiB is forty ReserveFreeGiB is eight and MonitorIntervalSeconds is two
  + retain the exact workspace test and Clippy semantic selections from P0
  + require offline tests format diff evidence and static audit without executing Cargo during P1 proof

